Obligations and gates both block, but they are not the same: gates are
\emph{pre-planned} checkpoints the user authors on an edge ("review before
fitting the hierarchical model"); obligations are \emph{evidence-driven} and
arise dynamically from summaries.
}
\section{Scopes}{

Decisions and obligations carry a scope: \code{project} (whole project) or
\verb{branch:<id>} (one branch). A decision recorded on a branch does not
satisfy a project-scope obligation, and vice versa. Use
\code{\link[=bg_next_actions]{bg_next_actions()}} to see what is outstanding at the relevant scope.
}

\section{Evidence freshness}{

A summary is \emph{fresh} when its fingerprint matches the node's current
configuration, \emph{stale} when the node's params, upstream inputs, or
environment changed since it was written. Packs consume fresh summaries by
default; a stale summary produces no obligation until the node is rerun.
}

